From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rog5 <rog5@localhost>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:17:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rog5: powerManager: Lock on idle-blank again (GNOME 49+
 _becomeModal)

The idle-blank action checked Main.screenShield._becomeModal()'s return
value to detect a failed grab. Since e350a7f1b ('screenShield: Drop seat
state check after grabs', GNOME 49) it returns nothing, so the check always
failed: the shell showed 'Unable to lock', skipped the lock and, when the
user came back, deactivated the shield. An idle phone on external power (no
policy suspend, which locks through suspend-forced) stayed unlocked. Check
the shield's grab instead.
---
 js/misc/powerManager.js | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/js/misc/powerManager.js b/js/misc/powerManager.js
index 821e015c4..5690af701 100644
--- a/js/misc/powerManager.js
+++ b/js/misc/powerManager.js
@@ -842,7 +842,12 @@ log("POWERMANAGER: turn on this._fadeInTimeout " + this._fadeInTimeout + " this.
 
                 // try to become modal now already, so that we fail before LOCK_DELAY
                 // in case becoming modal fails
-                if (!Main.screenShield._becomeModal()) {
+                // ROG5: since e350a7f1b ("screenShield: Drop seat state check
+                // after grabs", GNOME 49) _becomeModal() returns nothing, so
+                // testing its result always took this branch: idle-blank never
+                // locked, and user activity then deactivated the shield.
+                Main.screenShield._becomeModal();
+                if (!Main.screenShield._grab) {
                     Main.notifyError(
                         _('Unable to lock'),
                         _('Lock was blocked by an app'));
